MView Day 24 (2026-10-05)
=========================

Microscope files (looked at, nothing built yet)
-----------------------------------------------
The SP8 files in test\images\Microscope images are LAS X "export with
overlays" TIFFs: 8-bit RGB with the colour table applied and the 25 um
bar and time stamp drawn into the pixels. Their only size fields say
72 dpi in every file, whatever the image size (a placeholder): no pixel
size and no Leica data in them. The drawn bars give a check: Series084
(1024 px) 25 um = 191 px = 0.131 um/px; Glu...Image003 (2464 px) 290 px
= 0.086 um/px. The calibration is in the .lif / .lei (or a raw-data
export's MetaData XML). The user is getting the .lei files; measurement,
scale bar and metadata wait for them. Plan in specs\wanted features.txt
(user's draft).

Icon preview beside the sort panel (user)
-----------------------------------------
"if, in the right menu panel, the mouse is above a directory AND an icon
is assigned, display a larger version, if appropriate the original icon
size ... in a small picture to the left of the side bar."
- TSortPanel: OnSlotPreview; while a button with an icon is hovered, the
  panel and a box with the icon become one picture (FOut), FPreviewW
  wider on the left; Left moves left, hit tests and the folder menu use
  the new PanelLeft. The box takes no clicks.
- Size: the icon's own size (TSortIcons.NativeSize: the largest picture
  in the .ico, or the .png's), at least 128 px, at most 256 px (scaled
  for the screen) and what fits; under it the file name and own size.
- Review (independent) before delivery: compiles as far as can be told;
  two small fixes (no preview when there is room for less than 96 px;
  the box's frame on whole pixels, corners scaled).
Units changed: uSortPanel, uSortIcons, uMView. Spec §9.7.

