The info line's parts in the ini (user)
---------------------------------------
"text font, a list of items displayed in the status bar with 0/1 ...
the order of these entries should be the order in which they appear in
the status line. the entries =0 are just omitted."
- [InfoLine]: Font, FontSize (points; info line only), then FileName,
  Dimensions, Folder, Position, Videos, Sorting, Zoom, State, Animation,
  Filters, Messages, each 1 / 0, shown in the order of their lines
  (TConfig.ReadInfoLine reads the section's keys in file order; Save
  writes existing keys in place, new ones at the end).
- TMView.UpdateInfo builds the line from TConfig.InfoItems; the zoom
  ("52 % = W x H", angle) is the renderer's, so TMView puts
  InfoZoomMarker where it goes and TRenderer.InfoLine fills it in.
- Both renderers draw the info line in its own font (CPU: canvas font;
  GL: UpdateBar with the font, the bar's key includes it).
Units changed: uConfig, uMView, uRenderer, uGLRenderer. Spec §8.6, §14.

The rotation in "Apply filters to a copy" (user)
------------------------------------------------
"the right menu entry 'apply filters to a copy' should also transfer
the rotation state."
- The copy is turned in its pixels after the filters and the mirror:
  quarter turns exactly (RotateCW / CCW / 180), other angles bilinear
  on a larger canvas with black corners (uFilterImage.RotatedBitmap,
  clockwise as on screen); the full size follows (swapped for odd
  quarter turns). Name: ..._rot90; shown upright afterwards (before, the
  view was only turned again). Enabled also for a turn alone; the menu
  says "Apply filters and rotation to a copy" while the view is turned.
Units changed: uFilterImage, uMView, umainform. Spec §9.8.

Bug: a sort folder "C:\" opened MView's own folder (user)
----------------------------------------------------------
"i created the side folder 'c:\' ... if i gesture to change into the dir,
i get 'No images found in c:\projects\mview\build'"
- Folders are kept without their trailing backslash, so the drive root
  became "C:"; ExpandFileName("C:") is the current folder on drive C
  (MView's build folder), not the root. TNavigator.FullPath: a bare
  drive gets its backslash before ExpandFileName; used where a path
  comes in (TNavigator.OpenPath, TDirectoryScanner.Resolve).
Units changed: uNavigator, uDirectoryScanner.

No subfolders from a drive root (user)
--------------------------------------
"this calls imho for an ini setting to limit this behaviour ... 'do not
recurse from root'. this should also apply when the recursion 'climb up'
reaches root"
- [Navigation] RecurseFromDriveRoot=0 (default): a drive root (C:\, or a
  network share's root \\server\share), or an image directly in one, is
  opened without its subfolders even with Recursive=1; 1 = as any other
  folder. Decided in TMView.OpenMedia (OpensDriveRoot, by the name only),
  so it holds for every way in: a sort folder, the command line, Total
  Commander, the parent-folder command, and climbing (which already
  stops one level below the drive).
Units changed: uConfig, uMView. Spec §14.

